  <body>

    <%- include('../common-new/navbar') %>

      <div>

        <section class="hero-section pb-5 new-header-padding-sec">
          <div class="container">
            <div class="row flex-lg-row-reverse align-items-center g-4">
              <div class="col-lg-6">
                <img
                  src="https://assets.clarisco.com/clarisco-images/blockchain/industries/blockchain-iot-development/blockchain-iot-development-company.webp"
                  alt="blockchain-iot-development-company" />
              </div>
              <div class="col-lg-6">

                <h1 class="display-5 fw-bold lh-1 my-3">Best Blockchain <span class="fc-b">IoT</span> Development
                  Company </h1>
                <p> Internet of Things integrated with Blockchain to provide better solutions for
                  any problem you may be
                  faced with.</p>
                <div class="d-grid gap-2 d-md-flex justify-content-md-start">
                  <button data-bs-toggle="modal" data-bs-target="#PopForm"
                    class="nft-new-banner-button-1">Get a Demo</button>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="border-bottom-new-design py-5">
          <div class="container">
            <div class="row align-items-center g-4">
              <div class="col-lg-6">
                <img
                  src="https://assets.clarisco.com/clarisco-images/blockchain/industries/blockchain-iot-development/blockchain-iot-development.webp"
                  alt="blockchain-iot-development-1" />
              </div>
              <div class="col-lg-6">
                <h2 class="mb-4">Blockchain is the Future of IoT Company</h2>
                <p>Clarisco Solution is now active in the Internet of Things (IoT) field. The IoT
                  has made a significant
                  impact on distributed ledger technology and blockchain technology. We strive to create the perfect
                  distributed network of devices using IoT solutions. IoT solutions can be used to provide
                  interoperability solutions to Blockchains, ledgers and exchanges.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="py-5 border-bottom-new-design">
          <div class="container">
            <h2 class="text-center mb-5">The steps involved in Blockchain IoT</h2>
            <div class="row row-cols-1 row-cols-lg-3 g-4">
              <div class="col">
                <div class="card h-100">
                  <div class="card-body">
                    <i class="fa-solid fa-layer-group fs-24 fc-b"></i>
                    <h6 class="card-title mt-2">Identify the problem and define it</h6>
                    <p class="card-text">IoT is about finding solutions to problems that are posed by
                      blockchain technology. First, identify the problem and determine its extent.</p>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>
              <div class="col">
                <div class="card h-100">
                  <div class="card-body">
                    <i class="fa-solid fa-layer-group fs-24 fc-b"></i>
                    <h6 class="card-title mt-2">Fabricate Solution</h6>
                    <p class="card-text">Once the problem is defined, solutions can be found and used to
                      arrive at a solution.</p>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>
              <div class="col">
                <div class="card h-100">
                  <div class="card-body">
                    <i class="fa-solid fa-layer-group fs-24 fc-b"></i>
                    <h6 class="card-title mt-2">Get the Solution to create an app</h6>
                    <p class="card-text">Make an app or other asset to test the solution.</p>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>
              <div class="col">
                <div class="card h-100">
                  <div class="card-body">
                    <i class="fa-solid fa-layer-group fs-24 fc-b"></i>
                    <h6 class="card-title mt-2">Use the app</h6>
                    <p class="card-text">Once the app or asset has been created, it's time to implement the
                      problem and test the theory to determine if the solution works.</p>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>
              <div class="col">
                <div class="card h-100">
                  <div class="card-body">
                    <i class="fa-solid fa-layer-group fs-24 fc-b"></i>
                    <h6 class="card-title mt-2">Help and Improvement</h6>
                    <p class="card-text">Users are enjoying the results of the app or asset running
                      smoothly without any problems. Continuous support is provided to improve the asset or app.</p>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>

            </div>

          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="py-5 border-bottom-new-design">
          <div class="container">
            <h2 class="text-center mb-3">Solutions</h2>
            <p class="text-center mb-5">Some of the solutions offered by Blockchain IoT are as follows,</p>
            <div class="row row-cols-1 row-cols-lg-2 g-4">
              <div class="col">
                <div class="card h-100">
                  <div class="card-body">
                    <i class="fa-solid fa-layer-group fs-24 fc-b"></i>
                    <h6 class="card-title mt-2">Decentralization</h6>
                    <p class="card-text">Reduce transaction fees and eliminate peer-to-peer requirements in
                      blockchains</p>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>
              <div class="col">
                <div class="card h-100">
                  <div class="card-body">
                    <i class="fa-solid fa-layer-group fs-24 fc-b"></i>
                    <h6 class="card-title mt-2">Blockless distributed ledger</h6>
                    <p class="card-text">You can identify and approve transactions in the distributed
                      ledger, without using the blockchain.</p>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>
              <div class="col">
                <div class="card h-100">
                  <div class="card-body">
                    <i class="fa-solid fa-layer-group fs-24 fc-b"></i>
                    <h6 class="card-title mt-2">Blockchain as a Service (BaaS).</h6>
                    <p class="card-text">Cloud services can be integrated with Blockchain to quickly deploy
                      projects.</p>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>
              <div class="col">
                <div class="card h-100">
                  <div class="card-body">
                    <i class="fa-solid fa-layer-group fs-24 fc-b"></i>
                    <h6 class="card-title mt-2">Private entities and shared devices</h6>
                    <p class="card-text">You can share wireless devices that are connected to IoT or you
                      can buy private entities using Blockchain-connected IoT solutions.</p>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>


            </div>

          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="py-5 border-bottom-new-design">
          <div class="container">
            <h2 class="text-center mb-5">FAQ(Frequently Asked Question)</h2>
            <div class="accordion" id="accordionExample">
              <div class="accordion-item">
                <h2 class="accordion-header" id="headingOne">
                  <button class="accordion-button" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#collapseOne"
                    aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="collapseOne">
                    What is blockchain IoT?
                  </button>
                </h2>
                <div id="collapseOne" class="accordion-collapse collapse show" aria-labelledby="headingOne"
                  data-bs-parent="#accordionExample">
                  <div class="accordion-body">
                    Blockchain is a distributed ledger technology that combines IoT and blockchain to make
                    machine-to-machine transactions possible. It uses a set of transactions that are recorded in a
                    database, verified by multiple sources and entered into a common ledger distributed across all
                    nodes. It is based on a collection of transactions that have been recorded in a database and
                    verified by multiple sources. The transactions are then entered into a common ledger across all
                    nodes.</div>
                </div>
              </div>
              <div class="accordion-item">
                <h2 class="accordion-header" id="headingTwo">
                  <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse"
                    data-bs-target="#collapseTwo" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="collapseTwo">
                    What is the use of blockchain in IoT?
                  </button>
                </h2>
                <div id="collapseTwo" class="accordion-collapse collapse" aria-labelledby="headingTwo"
                  data-bs-parent="#accordionExample">
                  <div class="accordion-body">
                    What is the relationship between IoT and blockchain? IoT allows devices to communicate with each
                    other over the Internet and create secure records that can be used to verify transactions. IBM
                    Blockchain allows your business partners to access and share IoT data without central management.
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>
              <div class="accordion-item">
                <h2 class="accordion-header" id="headingThree">
                  <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse"
                    data-bs-target="#collapseThree" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="collapseThree">
                    IoT Blockchain System: What are some examples?
                  </button>
                </h2>
                <div id="collapseThree" class="accordion-collapse collapse" aria-labelledby="headingThree"
                  data-bs-parent="#accordionExample">
                  <div class="accordion-body">
                    NetObjex. How they are using blockchain in IoT. NetObjex created a standard, decentralized way for
                    IoT devices and other devices to communicate. The IoT Token, a blockchain-enabled token from the
                    company, provides a secure digital platform that allows smart devices within the same ecosystem to
                    communicate and interact with each other. </div>
                </div>
              </div>
              <div class="accordion-item">
                <h2 class="accordion-header" id="headingFour">
                  <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse"
                    data-bs-target="#collapseFour" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="collapseFour">
                    Blockchain can accelerate Internet of Things IoT adoption
                  </button>
                </h2>
                <div id="collapseFour" class="accordion-collapse collapse" aria-labelledby="headingFour"
                  data-bs-parent="#accordionExample">
                  <div class="accordion-body">
                    Blockchain storage of IoT data will add a layer of security that hackers would have to bypass to
                    gain access to the network. Blockchain offers a stronger level of encryption, making it nearly
                    impossible to overwrite data records.
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>
              <div class="accordion-item">
                <h2 class="accordion-header" id="headingFive">
                  <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse"
                    data-bs-target="#collapseFive" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="collapseFive">
                    Is blockchain an example of IoT?
                  </button>
                </h2>
                <div id="collapseFive" class="accordion-collapse collapse" aria-labelledby="headingFive"
                  data-bs-parent="#accordionExample">
                  <div class="accordion-body">
                    Blockchain eliminates the problems associated with the traditional centralized approach to
                    exchanging information generated by IoT devices. Telstra is one of the most prominent blockchain IoT
                    examples in smart homes.
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>



